{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-indent: -18pt;&quot;&gt;The\r\nproposed development would be inappropriately configured with the proposed\r\nbedroom 1 at ground floor stacked over by the first-floor kitchen/dining area, which\r\nwould result in adverse noise impact from vertical stacking issues and would\r\ncumulatively result in sub-standard level of living accommodation for the\r\nfuture occupiers of the proposed dwellings. The proposed development would\r\ntherefore be contrary to the high quality design aspirations of the National\r\nPlanning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D3 D .7 of the London Plan, Policies\r\nDM1 C, DM1 D (g), DM26 A (b) and DM26 E of the Harrow Development Management\r\nPolicies Local Plan (2013) and the Adopted Supplementary Planning Document:\r\nResidential Design Guide (2010).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;The\r\nproposed first floor side extension’s roof form in conjunction with the side dormers\r\nby reason of its poor design would create a poorly conceived, incongruous and\r\ncontrived form of development that fails to appropriately relate or respond to\r\nthe original dwellinghouse. The proposal&amp;nbsp;would give rise to a\r\ndisproportionate addition which would fail to provide a coherent pattern of\r\ndevelopment in the street scene, and would therefore unduly harm the form,\r\nopenness and proportion of the site and relationship with the properties in the\r\nlocality. The proposal would be unduly harmful to the character and appearance\r\nof the original dwellinghouse and the visual amenities of the area,\r\n&amp;nbsp;contrary to the high quality design aspirations of the National Planning\r\nPolicy Framework (2024), Policy D3 D(1) and D(11) of The&amp;nbsp; London Plan\r\n(2021), Core Policy CS1.B of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012), Policy DM1 of the\r\nDevelopment Management Plan Local Policies (2013) and the Adopted Supplementary\r\nPlanning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
